00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:38.820
So, how can we solve this logic problem? We'll start out by evaluating each of the statements.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.820
First consider statement 1: all of the below.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:49.700
If statement 1 is true that implies all of the statements below, including 5, are true.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:58.200
But if statement 5 is true, that means none of the statements above 5 can be true, including statement 1.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.900
That would imply statement 1 has to be false.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.920
This means 1 is a self contradicting statement and cannot be true.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.160
So we'll mark that statement 1 cannot be true.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.540
Now, let's skip statement 2 for a second and consider 3: all of the above.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.640
If 3 is true that implies 1 is true.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.460
But we already concluded 1 is self-contradictory and cannot be true.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.220
This means 3 also cannot be true

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.660
Now, let's go to statement 2: none of the below.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:43.600
if statement 2 is true that implies statement 4 has to be false.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.360
4 Says that one of the above is true.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.920
So if 4 is false, that means none of the above can be true.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:02.820
So if 4 is false, since one and three are already known to be false, we must have that two is false.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:09.380
Hence we have that 2 is a self contradictory statement and also cannot be true.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.520
Now, consider statement 4.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.720
If 4 is true, then 1, 2, or 3 has to be true.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:25.080
But we already concluded that 1, 2, &amp; 3 cannot be true. This means statement 4 has to be false.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:31.840
Now let's skip statement 5 for a second and go to statement 6: none of the above.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:36.920
If 6 is true, then 5 has to be false.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:41.600
Implying some statement 1, 2, 3, or 4 has to be true.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:51.520
But we already know 1, 2, 3, &amp; 4 are false so statement 6 cannot be a true statement.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:59.500
So now we're left with statement 5: none of the above. Can 5 be true?

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.220
Yes it can!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:08.160
If 5 is true, we would need 1, 2, 3, &amp; 4 to be false, which we already worked out.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:12.380
So there's no contradiction if we have that 5 is a true statement.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.820
So the correct answer is 5.

